configfile: no deprecation warning for the Anycubic stock MCU firmware

ShedNaja runs the Anycubic stock MCU firmware v1.4.3 on purpose (no reflash).
It lacks STEPPER_STEP_BOTH_EDGE, which klippy reports as "deprecated code ...
Recompiling and flashing is recommended" on every start. Log it instead.

--- a/klippy/configfile.py
+++ b/klippy/configfile.py
@@ -531,6 +531,13 @@
         self._add_deprecated(res)
     def deprecate_mcu_code(self, mcu, feature, msg=None):
         mcu_name = mcu.get_name()
+        # Kobra S1: the Anycubic stock MCU firmware (v1.x) is the supported default and is
+        # not reflashed, so its older protocol (e.g. no STEPPER_STEP_BOTH_EDGE) is logged,
+        # not reported as a warning that asks to recompile and flash
+        if mcu.get_status()['mcu_version'].strip('"').startswith('v1.'):
+            logging.info("MCU '%s' (Anycubic stock firmware %s) lacks feature '%s'",
+                         mcu_name, mcu.get_status()['mcu_version'], feature)
+            return
         if msg is None:
             vhost = self.printer.start_args['software_version']
             vmcu = mcu.get_status()['mcu_version']
